  "control_limits_en": "No limit line in the cited sources; reference point(s) only, open edges. South Arabian period of the 5th–4th c. BCE marked by the Yeha temple (GHA II ch.13 pp.343, 345); kings styled 'mukarrib of D'iamat and Saba'' over clans of the northern Ethiopian highlands (pp.353–354). Punt itself is unlocated ('boundaries uncertain', GHA II ch.4 pp.144–145) and is not marked. Dates −500/−400 are display values for the 5th–4th c. Open edges: no limit line in the source; not a border.",
